From 9398a9e33c3ce9816226f2feef7bc2e942bf406c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:22:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kernels: tests of the prediction and of two materials, review
 fixes

BatchIntegrationTest:
- the prediction of each time step is recorded (resolution without
  iteration, then revert) and compared;
- a cube loaded by an imposed pressure, for which the inner forces at
  the beginning of a time step contribute to the prediction (dropping
  them from the prediction computed by kernels is now detected);
- a cube made of two materials (new mesh cube-two-materials.mesh, the
  periodic mesh cube_2mat_per.mesh identifying the faces x = 0 and
  x = 1), the second one being integrated on the host while the first
  one is integrated on the device;
- the linear elastic behaviour, whose material properties vary from one
  point to another, generated by the generic-parallel interface (copies
  of the material properties on the device), and the computations by
  kernels with a prediction for the behaviours of the generic-parallel
  interface;
- the material properties of this behaviour are also given at the
  beginning of the time step for a prediction, which integrates the
  behaviour at the beginning of the time step.

The tests on the GPU are not run at the same time: each process may
reserve a large memory pool. The assembly of the stiffness matrices by
kernels refuses a number of threads exceeding the range of int.
